CitiAI hands every customer one Skeid client key. The operator assigns MCP servers to a customer key ID in the config; the customer wires each assigned server into its client (Hermes Agent, Claude Code, Codex) with that same key. Skeid is a thin authenticating reverse proxy for MCP Streamable HTTP: relayed, not translated (ADR 0021), no tool aggregation, no understanding of the protocol.

Wanted:

- POST|GET|DELETE /mcp/<name> (and sub-paths) relayed to the configured upstream URL, behind client authentication like /v1/*
- the server has to be assigned to the customer key ID; unknown or unassigned name is 404 (existence is not revealed), no or wrong key is 401
- the client Authorization never goes upstream; the upstream credential comes from the key broker or an environment variable, never from the config text or a log line
- body untouched; Content-Type, Accept, Mcp-Session-Id, Mcp-Protocol-Version, Last-Event-ID passed on; status, Mcp-Session-Id and a text/event-stream answer relayed unbuffered, under the upstream timeout of an LLM stream
- GET /v1/mcp/servers lists only the servers assigned to the presented key, with the public URL and never the upstream URL or its headers; transport: stdio entries are hints for a server on the customer machine and are not proxied
- config section mcp: (public URL, servers with url, description, key source, keys); without it Skeid behaves exactly as before
- usage event per relayed request if it fits the store without bending it

Not in scope: tool aggregation, starting stdio processes, per-end-user OAuth, an admin API for assignments, deployment.

